<title>THAILAND: Thai 1997/98 soybean output revised upwards.</title>
<headline>Thai 1997/98 soybean output revised upwards.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Thailand's Agriculture Ministry on Monday raised the 1997/98 (April-March) soybean output projection to 397,000 tonnes from 383,628 tonnes set earlier.  </p>
<p>The planting area was revised slightly upwards to 282,880 hectares from 278,984 seen earlier. The yield also edged up marginally to 1.40 tonnes per hectare from 1.38 tonnes in a previous projection.</p>
<p>Despite the improvement, local soymeal supply still trailed far behind demand, which exceeds one million tonnes a year. Thailand earlier this year removed import quotas and tariffs on soybean imports.</p>
<p>The following are annual Thai government soybean crop statistics (in tonnes):</p>
<p>1985-86  309,000   1986-87  356,000</p>
<p>1987-88  338,000   1988-89  516,811   1989-90  672,368</p>
<p>1990-91  530,112   1991-92  435,587   1992-93  480-148</p>
<p>1993-94  513-099   1994-95  527-581   1995-96  451,461</p>
<p>1996-97  352,279   1997-98  397,000 (forecast)</p>
<p>    Crop year: April-March   Major areas: Sukhothai, Loei</p>
<p>Nakhon Sawan, Phitsanulok Khamphaeng Phet   Water source: Rain</p>
<p>(1st crop) Irrigation (2nd crop)   -- Bangkok newsroom (662)</p>
<p>652-0642</p>
